    "photo_didentite": [
      {
        "texteAccordeon": "<p>If you apply with a paper application, an official passport photo for Australia should be</p>\n<ul>\n<li>35mm-40mm wide and 45mm-50mm high,</li>\n<li>your head must be a maximum of 36mm and a minimum of 32mm from chin to crown.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If you apply for an official document online, the digital photo should match the printed photo in size and all other requirements.</p>\n",
        "titre_accordeon": "What size is a passport photo in Australia?"
      },
      {
        "texteAccordeon": "<aside class=\"kal-accordion-item-active-aside\">Yes! You can take your own passport photo. You can do it with the back camera of your phone, but make sure that you are following all the guidelines to have your photo accepted (lighting, shadow, background color). You can also use the Smartphone iD tool that does everything for you. Simply choose your country and document, take a photo, and receive it later in email. It’s that easy!</aside>\n",
        "titre_accordeon": "Can you take a passport photo on your phone?"
      },
      {
        "texteAccordeon": "<aside class=\"kal-accordion-item-active-aside\">To print passport photos with your PC, you must first download software that allows you to obtain 35mm x 45mm photos. Then, you will have to connect a printer compatible with photo paper to your PC because only professionally printed passport photos are accepted.If you don&#8217;t want to download any software or skip the trouble of searching for an easy tool online, you can opt for the Smartphone iD service, where you only need to choose the needed document type and everything else is done for you. You can receive a professional 10x15cm print to your doorstep or use the 10x15cm digital file we send to email and use it in a printing facility nearby.</p>\n</aside>\n",
        "titre_accordeon": "How to print a passport size photo?"
      },
      {
        "texteAccordeon": "<aside class=\"kal-accordion-item-active-aside\">To print passport photos with your PC, you must first download software that allows you to obtain 35mm x 45mm photos. Then, you will have to connect a printer compatible with photo paper to your PC because only professionally printed passport photos are accepted.If you don&#8217;t want to download any software or skip the trouble of searching for an easy tool online, you can opt for the Smartphone iD service, where you only need to choose the needed document type and everything else is done for you. You can receive a professional 10x15cm print to your doorstep or use the 10x15cm digital file we send to email and use it in a printing facility nearby.</p>\n</aside>\n",
